Here is a complete step-by-step guide to create a VS Code Extension + how to upgrade it properly 👇

🚀 PART 1: Create VS Code Extension (Full Steps)
✅ Step 1: Install required tools

Install Node.js:

https://nodejs.org

Install VS Code Extension Generator:

npm install -g yo generator-code
✅ Step 2: Create new extension

Run:

yo code

Then select:

👉 New Extension Pack (if you are making your current project)
OR
👉 New Extension (if starting fresh)

Fill details:

Name → your extension name
Publisher → your VS Code publisher ID
Description → short description
Git → yes/no
✅ Step 3: Open project in VS Code
cd your-extension-folder
code .
✅ Step 4: Understand main files
📦 package.json (most important)

Contains:

name
version
extensionPack (your list)
metadata
📁 extensionPack (your case)

For extension packs:

"extensionPack": [
  "extension.id.here"
]
✅ Step 5: Add icon (optional but recommended)

Add:

images/icon.png

Then in package.json:

"icon": "images/icon.png"
✅ Step 6: Test extension locally

Press:

F5

This opens:
👉 Extension Development Host

✅ Step 7: Install VSCE (publisher tool)
npm install -g @vscode/vsce
✅ Step 8: Login to marketplace
vsce login your-publisher-name
✅ Step 9: Package extension
vsce package

This creates:

your-extension.vsix
✅ Step 10: Publish extension
vsce publish
🔁 PART 2: How to Upgrade Extension (VERY IMPORTANT)

Every update follows this rule:

✅ Step 1: Increase version

Example:

First release:
"version": "0.0.1"
Next update:
"version": "0.0.2"

or

"version": "0.1.0"

👉 NEVER reuse old version number

✅ Step 2: Make your changes

Examples:

add/remove extensions in extensionPack
update description
change icon
fix metadata
✅ Step 3: Rebuild package
vsce package
✅ Step 4: Publish update
vsce publish
⚠️ IMPORTANT RULES (very important for your case)
❌ You CANNOT:
reuse same version (0.0.1 again)
reuse deleted extension name after unpublish
publish without incrementing version
✅ You MUST:
always increase version
keep same publisher
keep same extension name for updates
🧠 Simple Upgrade Flow
Edit code
   ↓
Increase version
   ↓
vsce package
   ↓
vsce publish